---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const article = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'Article',
  headline: 'Canada Visitor Visa from Pakistan — Complete 2026 Guide',
  author: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'VisaPath.pk' },
  publisher: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'VisaPath.pk' },
  datePublished: '2026-10-24',
};

const faq = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'FAQPage',
  mainEntity: [
    { '@type': 'Question', name: 'How long is Canada visitor visa valid?',
      acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: 'Canada visitor visas are usually issued as multiple-entry valid up to 10 years or until passport expiry, whichever is earlier. Each entry allows up to 6 months stay.' } },
    { '@type': 'Question', name: 'What is the Super Visa?',
      acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: 'The Super Visa is a special visitor visa for parents and grandparents of Canadian citizens or permanent residents. It allows stays of up to 5 years per entry.' } },
    { '@type': 'Question', name: 'Can I apply for Canada visa online from Pakistan?',
      acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: 'Yes. Pakistani applicants apply online via the IRCC portal and give biometrics at VFS Global centres in Islamabad, Lahore, or Karachi.' } },
  ],
};
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Canada Visitor Visa from Pakistan — Complete 2026 Guide"
  description="How Pakistanis apply for Canada visitor (TRV) visa in 2026. Documents, biometrics, Super Visa, processing times, refusal reasons."
  schema={[article, faq]}
>
  <article class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 py-10">
    <nav class="text-sm text-gray-500 mb-4">
      <a href="/" class="hover:text-brand-600">Home</a> ›
      <a href="/guides/" class="hover:text-brand-600">Guides</a> ›
      <span>Canada Visitor Visa</span>
    </nav>

    <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold mb-4">Canada Visitor Visa from Pakistan — Complete 2026 Guide</h1>
    <p class="text-gray-500 text-sm mb-8">Last updated: October 2026 · 10 minute read</p>

    <section class="prose max-w-none">
      <p class="lead text-lg">
        A Canada Visitor Visa (also called Temporary Resident Visa or TRV) lets Pakistani passport holders visit Canada for tourism, visiting family, business meetings, or short events. This guide covers who can apply, what you need, and how to maximise approval chances.
      </p>

      <h2>Types of Visitor Visa</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Single-entry:</strong> allows one entry to Canada before expiry</li>
        <li><strong>Multiple-entry:</strong> allows unlimited entries up to 10 years (or passport expiry); each visit up to 6 months</li>
        <li><strong>Super Visa:</strong> special category for parents and grandparents of Canadian citizens/PRs; stays up to 5 years per entry</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Most approved Pakistani visitor visas are issued as multiple-entry valid up to the passport's expiry.
      </p>

      <h2>Who Can Apply</h2>
      <p>You must:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Have a valid Pakistani passport</li>
        <li>Convince an officer you'll leave Canada at the end of your visit</li>
        <li>Have enough money for your stay</li>
        <li>Have no criminal record</li>
        <li>Be in good health (medical exam may be required for stays over 6 months)</li>
        <li>Not pose a security risk</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Documents Required</h2>
      <h3>Core Application</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>Completed IMM 5257 application form</li>
        <li>Family Information form (IMM 5645)</li>
        <li>Current passport + all previous passports</li>
        <li>2 passport photos (Canadian specification)</li>
        <li>CNIC + Family Registration Certificate</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>Financial Proof</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>Bank statements — last 4 months with stamp</li>
        <li>Salary slips — last 3 months</li>
        <li>Tax returns — last 2 years</li>
        <li>Property documents (if applicable)</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>Employment / Business</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>Employment letter stating position, salary, duration, approved leave</li>
        <li>Business registration (if self-employed)</li>
        <li>SECP, NTN, tax returns for business</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>Purpose of Trip</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>Letter of invitation from Canadian host (if visiting someone)</li>
        <li>Host's immigration status copy (citizenship card, PR card, work permit)</li>
        <li>Host's bank statements and employment proof (if sponsoring your stay)</li>
        <li>Travel itinerary and hotel bookings</li>
        <li>Return flight reservation</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Fees</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Visa fee:</strong> CAD $100 (approximately PKR 20,500)</li>
        <li><strong>Biometrics fee:</strong> CAD $85 (approximately PKR 17,500)</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Pay online via IRCC portal using a credit card. Fees are non-refundable.
      </p>

      <h2>Application Process</h2>
      <h3>Step 1 — Create IRCC Account</h3>
      <p>
        Go to <code>canada.ca/en/immigration-refugees-citizenship</code>. Create a "GCKey" account or sign in via "Sign-In Partner" (not available in Pakistan).
      </p>

      <h3>Step 2 — Complete Online Application</h3>
      <p>
        Answer the "Come to Canada" questionnaire. Based on your answers, you'll be routed to the appropriate TRV application forms. Upload all documents, review, and pay fees.
      </p>

      <h3>Step 3 — Give Biometrics</h3>
      <p>
        After paying the biometrics fee, you receive a Biometric Instruction Letter (BIL). Within 30 days, book an appointment at VFS Global Canada Visa Application Centre in Islamabad, Lahore, or Karachi.
      </p>

      <h3>Step 4 — Processing</h3>
      <p>
        Current processing time for Canada visitor visa from Pakistan is typically <strong>4–8 weeks</strong> after biometrics. During peak periods, this can extend to 12 weeks.
      </p>

      <h3>Step 5 — Submit Passport</h3>
      <p>
        If approved, you receive a passport request letter. Submit your passport to the VFS centre; the visa (counterfoil) is affixed and your passport returned via courier.
      </p>

      <h2>Super Visa for Parents and Grandparents</h2>
      <p>
        If your child or grandchild is a Canadian citizen or permanent resident, you can apply for the <strong>Super Visa</strong> instead of a regular TRV. Benefits:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Up to 5 years per entry (vs. 6 months for regular TRV)</li>
        <li>Valid up to 10 years</li>
        <li>Multiple entries</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Super Visa requirements:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Letter of invitation from your child/grandchild in Canada</li>
        <li>Proof they meet minimum income threshold (based on LICO)</li>
        <li>Private medical insurance from a Canadian company, valid at least 1 year, minimum CAD $100,000 coverage</li>
        <li>Immigration medical exam</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Common Refusal Reasons</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Weak ties to Pakistan</strong> — officer not convinced you'll return</li>
        <li><strong>Insufficient funds</strong> — bank balance doesn't match trip cost</li>
        <li><strong>Travel history</strong> — no previous international travel</li>
        <li><strong>Purpose of visit unclear</strong> — vague letter of invitation</li>
        <li><strong>Immigration status of inviter</strong> — if host's status is unclear or expired</li>
        <li><strong>Previous overstays or refusals</strong> in other countries not disclosed</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>If Refused</h2>
      <p>
        Canada doesn't offer appeals for TRV refusals. You can:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Reapply</strong> addressing the reasons given in the refusal letter</li>
        <li><strong>Request GCMS notes</strong> through a Canadian lawyer or consultant to see detailed officer comments</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>After Arrival in Canada</h2>
      <p>
        At the airport, a CBSA officer stamps your passport. The length of stay granted is based on their assessment — typically 6 months, sometimes less. The stamp expiry is your actual authorised stay, which may differ from the visa validity.
      </p>

      <h2>Working or Studying on a Visitor Visa</h2>
      <p>
        You <strong>cannot</strong> work in Canada on a visitor visa. You can study only short courses (under 6 months) without a study permit. Longer studies require a Study Permit.
      </p>

      <h2>Extending Your Stay</h2>
      <p>
        To stay beyond the authorised date, apply for a Visitor Record extension at least 30 days before your current status expires. There's no guarantee of approval.
      </p>

      <h2>Related Resources</h2>
      <p>
        <a href="/tools/visa-fee-calculator/">Fee Calculator</a> ·
        <a href="/tools/document-checklist-generator/">Document Checklist</a> ·
        <a href="/tools/visa-processing-time/">Processing Times</a>
      </p>
    </section>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
